What buyers and answer engines are asking in 2026 that no URL answered
directly: refinish-vs-replace, wide-plank white oak, herringbone vs chevron,
stair timelines, refinish-vs-retread, durable stair finishes, winter
installs, pets, occupied refinishing, cure windows, runners. Each gets a
short answer in data/answers.ts (8 of 11 in the stairs/installation wedge,
keeping the concentration test honest), every one mapped to exactly one URL
in docs/QUERY-INVENTORY.md's new 2026 demand table. One new guide,
hardwood-flooring-trends-gta-2026, covers the trend queries (wide plank,
warm tones, matte, pattern floors, whole-house stair continuity; grey and
gloss fading) as specification advice with zero invented figures — its cost
section points at the published bands and the estimator.

Everything derives: the 12 new pages enter the sitemap, /llms.txt,
/llms-full.txt, the search index, FAQPage markup on /answers, and the
assistant corpus with no surface-specific edits. Derived counts updated
everywhere in the same commit (371 pages, 39 answers, 20 guides). Verify
green: typecheck, 168 tests, build 371 pages, audit clean.

No third-party feed ingestion, no loosened assistant, no new city, no new
service — per AGENTS.md rules 4, 5, and the assistant section.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
